{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit cap, interest and return deadline","requirement":"A lessor may not hold a security deposit above one month's rent, must keep it in a separate interest-bearing account, pay 5 per cent interest a year, and return it with an itemized damage list within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1 month's rent; 5% interest per year; return within 30 days","coverage_conditions":"Applies to leases of residential real property and to any lessor or successor in interest who accepts or holds a tenant's security deposit.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Successor-in-interest liability does not apply to a city or town acquiring title under chapter 60, or to a chartered foreclosing mortgagee or mortgagee in possession.","penalty":"Lessor forfeits the right to retain any deposit and owes three times the deposit plus 5 per cent interest from the date due, court costs and reasonable attorney's fees; failure to comply with the account or receipt rules entitles the tenant to immediate return.","effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent provided that such security deposit is deposited as required by subsection (3) and that the tenant is given the statement of condition as required by subsection (2)","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts cap on advance rent and upfront charges at tenancy start","requirement":"At or before the start of a tenancy, a lessor or the lessor's agent may not require a tenant or applicant to pay more than first month's rent, last month's rent, a one-month security deposit, and the cost of a key and lock.","key_value":"first month's rent + last month's rent + 1 month's rent deposit + key/lock cost","coverage_conditions":"Applies to any tenancy of residential real property; binding on the lessor and on the lessor's agent.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(b) At or prior to the commencement of any tenancy, no lessor or agent of the lessor may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay, to the lessor or to an agent of the lessor, any amount in excess of the following: (i) rent for the first full month of occupancy;  and, (ii) rent for the last full month of occupancy calculated at the same rate as the first month;  and,","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts fee-in-lieu-of-deposit option must be offered without regard to income or credit score","requirement":"A lessor who offers a fee in lieu of a security deposit must offer that option to every applicant approved for occupancy, regardless of income, credit score and other listed characteristics, and may not use those factors to set the fee.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Lessors who offer a fee in lieu of a security deposit, under regulations of the executive office of housing and livable communities.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(E) require a lessor who offers such a fee in lieu of security deposit:  (I) to offer the option of a fee in lieu of a security deposit to every prospective tenant whose application for occupancy has been approved, regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, size of household or credit score;","interaction":null,"confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
